    "abstract": "1 Pre-processing of input road network and junction data [in preparation for defining road nodes and their attributes] Code: 1.clip_spatial_inputs.py; 2.enrich_road_segments.pyS1.2.2 2 Processing of input traffic flow speed data [in preparation for deriving travel times on road nodes] Code: 3.process_speed_data.pyS1.2.3 3 Generation and harmonisation of processed input data for MATSDA's travel database [combining outputs of steps 1 and 2] Code: 4.London_private_graph_input.pyS1.2.",
    "field": "Urban transport modelling",
    "problem": "Existing transport models for urban climate studies are challenged by the need to dynamically represent realistic driver behavior, as the choice between using local versus major roads varies significantly with journey length and time of day, affecting the accuracy of traffic and emissions simulations.",
    "method": "This paper proposes a transport model using a graph-based travel database and Dijkstra's algorithm, with a distance-dependent local road parameterization, to simulate optimal vehicle routes and travel times for dynamic urban climate studies.",
    "task": "The task is to develop the MATSDA-roads v2.0 model, which creates a road travel database and pathfinding algorithm to simulate vehicle journeys for dynamic urban climate studies, using London as a case study.",
