    "innovation": "This paper presents MATSDA-roads v2.0, a transport model for dynamic urban climate studies that generates a detailed road travel database and pathfinding tool to simulate vehicle journeys, with a comprehensive development and evaluation for London.",
    "kg_extraction_triplets": [
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "MATSDA-roads v2.0",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "HAS_SOURCE_COMPONENT",
            "target_entity_instance": "MATSDA-roads Pathfinder v2.0",
            "target_entity_type": "SourceComponent",
            "paragraph": "The MATSDA-roads Pathfinder v2.0 (MATSDA_pathfinder.py, Table S9) calculates the optimal travel route through the MATSDA-roads travel database (\u00a7S1.3) for a given origin-destination grid cell pair. It loads the complete transport database, which represents all possible road segments and connections as nodes and journeys. For a given starting node (origin) and time interval, it applies Dijkstra's algorithm (Dijkstra 1959) to find the fastest route to every other node in the network (Fig. S3).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
